{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:06:55.265Z","ordinal":13090,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d773cf2d-9f66-4be7-8de1-e4743d78020d","process_id":"47282","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nd=json.loads(Path('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json').read_text())\nfor t in d['tasks']:\n if t['id'] in ['CSF-T002','CSF-T003','CSF-T004']:\n  print(json.dumps(t,indent=2))\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nd=json.loads(Path('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json').read_text())\nfor t in d['tasks']:\n if t['id'] in ['CSF-T002','CSF-T003','CSF-T004']:\n  print(json.dumps(t,indent=2))\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T002\",\n  \"title\": \"Qualify current versions, exports and strict enforcement\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"type\": \"foundation\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-001\",\n    \"CSF-002\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T001\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Resolve current official releases, including stable Effect module paths, then qualify one exact Bun/TypeScript/React/Atom/Alchemy/tooling graph in a fresh scratch fixture before integrating it.\",\n    \"Qualify the proposed exact Scheduler peer-metadata correction, or use a newer upstream fix. Preserve valid tax outputs; update package exports/types/imports and versioning consequences deliberately.\",\n    \"Adopt the complete canonical current repository skills (0.6.1 successor of the designed 0.6.0 baseline) and declared TaxKit profiles/receipts, including the required Linear skill folder and Claude link without creating provider projects/issues. Merge all eleven portable strict Effect rules, including no-imperative-collections, and workspace-export direction into the actual lint config across source/tests/tools/config/infrastructure. Reuse baseline mutation/loop/collection checks; add only evidenced gaps and readonly-value checks. Exact Promise-returning/runtime host exceptions do not exempt other constructs.\",\n    \"Extend actual-command positive/negative fixtures under moved paths; assert admitted file counts, exit codes and expected rules. Prove removing/disabling required rules or broadening exact assignment/method exceptions fails the verifier. Refresh Turbo read/input/cache ownership, Knip inventories and CI commands; keep explicit generated/vendor exclusions.\",\n    \"Qualify canonical rejection of let/var, assignments/writes/delete/updates, loops, native array traversal including forEach and mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, switch and manual tag checks. Use existing restrictions and focused corrections for Object/Reflect writes, mutable class/contract values, WeakMap/WeakSet and demonstrated destructured/local aliases. Computed member access is already rejected by no-unchecked-index. Accept persistent collections, pure immutable Effect-managed state and qualified Alchemy Output operations. Preserve/qualify stronger lexical runtime callback/reference checks outside exact hosts. Review helper purpose, Schema ownership and pipe/flat-program call graphs separately; lint alone is not semantic proof.\",\n    \"Cover owned .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files, including retained JavaScript policy tools, in actual lint scope; convert to checked TypeScript where necessary instead of treating the scaffold TypeScript-only override as complete. Executable MDX expressions/imports remain with the existing content-policy owner.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"package.json, bun.lock, turbo.json, tsconfig*, oxlint.config.ts, oxfmt.config.ts, Knip config and .github/workflows/quality.yml\",\n    \"tools/oxlint/** policy/fixtures, tools/effect-language-service/** and tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json\",\n    \"Canonical .agents/skills/** copies with explicit local profiles; AGENTS.md, README.md and affected package READMEs\",\n    \"Qualified version receipt, any exact-version patches/**, applicable .changeset/*.md and owning standards/architecture\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun install --frozen-lockfile\",\n    \"bun run format:check\",\n    \"bun run lint\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check:effect-language-service\",\n    \"bun run test:skills\",\n    \"bun run check:harness-governance\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Qualify Atom server rendering/hydration, scheduled/cancelled updates, rapid input changes, strict-mode remount and final disposal on the selected React/Scheduler graph.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n    \"Deliberate bad fixtures fail with the expected rule in every owned path group, and documented valid adapters pass.\",\n    \"Retained valid calculations produce unchanged golden results; breaking interfaces have an appropriate Changeset.\",\n    \"No owned application, domain, test, script or infrastructure workflow retains forbidden mutation or imperative loops. Every necessary host construct has an exact owner/containment/test/removal record; copied reference templates do not provide an escape for executable owned code.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-stable-dependency-qualification.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-version-observations.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-medicare-scope-conflict.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-canonical-skills.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-atom-qualification.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-workflow-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-binding-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-route-policy.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-enforcement-canaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lexical-policy-gaps.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-documentation-tools.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-evaluation-tools.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-artifacts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-credentials.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-workflow-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-receipt-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-file-deadlines.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-retained-deployment-proof.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-inventory-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-typed-lint-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-release-script-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-checking-scripts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-api-app-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-import-checker.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-runtime-tests.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-fixture-deadlines.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-app-hosts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-infrastructure-native-tests.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-web-app-hosts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-hosted-docs-native-proof.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-built-worker-proof.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n  \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-003\",\n    \"CSF-004\",\n    \"CSF-007\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n    \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n    \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n    \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n    \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n    \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n    \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n    \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n    \"bun run api:smoke\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n    \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n    \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n    \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n    \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n    \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n    \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n  \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-001\",\n    \"CSF-004\",\n    \"CSF-005\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Implement every existing catalogue calculator with immutable temporary input/report state, retaining tax rules/results and explicit 2025-26/PAYG limits. Use the Q10-Q12 choices: an explicit Calculate button; edits mark the old answer stale and cancel old work; a main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and sources; a calculator-first homepage with clear developer and agent routes.\",\n    \"Give the SDK an explicit caller-owned lifetime at its plain Promise boundary and an Effect interface; remove the package-global runtime and generic client escapes.\",\n    \"Complete named RPC and public HTTP/OpenAPI operations, bounded body/work/concurrency/rate policy and checked expected failures. Limits and the same safe application owner apply to every transport and caller.\",\n    \"Update package examples, generated snapshots, export/consumer fixtures, supported-scope public copy and Changesets with the new interface.\",\n    \"Tighten retained core/rule/calculator code to the accepted immutable/declarative policy, including one owning Schema and its whole-record checks, fallible constrained constructors, Option for semantic absence with historical codecs preserved, checked configuration, persistent collections, closed named services and flat piping. Do not re-decode checked internal values or use JSON cache keys. Preserve all valid known results; remove only unjustified helper wrappers and keep semantic operation owners.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/web calculator routes/feature containers/leaves and apps/api application operations\",\n    \"packages/calculators/**, packages/core/**, packages/rules/au/*/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/** and packages/sdk/typescript/** owning contracts/exports/tests/examples\",\n    \"Owning package/app READMEs, docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md, frontend.md, effect-services.md and appropriate .changeset/*.md\",\n    \"Local calculator/RPC/HTTP/OpenAPI/SDK consumer and privacy receipts\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/calculators test\",\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n    \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n    \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n    \"bun run api:smoke\",\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run changeset:status\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n    \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n    \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n    \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n    \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\"\n  ]\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T002\",\n  \"title\": \"Qualify current versions, exports and strict enforcement\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"type\": \"foundation\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-001\",\n    \"CSF-002\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T001\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Resolve current official releases, including stable Effect module paths, then qualify one exact Bun/TypeScript/React/Atom/Alchemy/tooling graph in a fresh scratch fixture before integrating it.\",\n    \"Qualify the proposed exact Scheduler peer-metadata correction, or use a newer upstream fix. Preserve valid tax outputs; update package exports/types/imports and versioning consequences deliberately.\",\n    \"Adopt the complete canonical current repository skills (0.6.1 successor of the designed 0.6.0 baseline) and declared TaxKit profiles/receipts, including the required Linear skill folder and Claude link without creating provider projects/issues. Merge all eleven portable strict Effect rules, including no-imperative-collections, and workspace-export direction into the actual lint config across source/tests/tools/config/infrastructure. Reuse baseline mutation/loop/collection checks; add only evidenced gaps and readonly-value checks. Exact Promise-returning/runtime host exceptions do not exempt other constructs.\",\n    \"Extend actual-command positive/negative fixtures under moved paths; assert admitted file counts, exit codes and expected rules. Prove removing/disabling required rules or broadening exact assignment/method exceptions fails the verifier. Refresh Turbo read/input/cache ownership, Knip inventories and CI commands; keep explicit generated/vendor exclusions.\",\n    \"Qualify canonical rejection of let/var, assignments/writes/delete/updates, loops, native array traversal including forEach and mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, switch and manual tag checks. Use existing restrictions and focused corrections for Object/Reflect writes, mutable class/contract values, WeakMap/WeakSet and demonstrated destructured/local aliases. Computed member access is already rejected by no-unchecked-index. Accept persistent collections, pure immutable Effect-managed state and qualified Alchemy Output operations. Preserve/qualify stronger lexical runtime callback/reference checks outside exact hosts. Review helper purpose, Schema ownership and pipe/flat-program call graphs separately; lint alone is not semantic proof.\",\n    \"Cover owned .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files, including retained JavaScript policy tools, in actual lint scope; convert to checked TypeScript where necessary instead of treating the scaffold TypeScript-only override as complete. Executable MDX expressions/imports remain with the existing content-policy owner.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"package.json, bun.lock, turbo.json, tsconfig*, oxlint.config.ts, oxfmt.config.ts, Knip config and .github/workflows/quality.yml\",\n    \"tools/oxlint/** policy/fixtures, tools/effect-language-service/** and tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json\",\n    \"Canonical .agents/skills/** copies with explicit local profiles; AGENTS.md, README.md and affected package READMEs\",\n    \"Qualified version receipt, any exact-version patches/**, applicable .changeset/*.md and owning standards/architecture\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun install --frozen-lockfile\",\n    \"bun run format:check\",\n    \"bun run lint\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check:effect-language-service\",\n    \"bun run test:skills\",\n    \"bun run check:harness-governance\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Qualify Atom server rendering/hydration, scheduled/cancelled updates, rapid input changes, strict-mode remount and final disposal on the selected React/Scheduler graph.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n    \"Deliberate bad fixtures fail with the expected rule in every owned path group, and documented valid adapters pass.\",\n    \"Retained valid calculations produce unchanged golden results; breaking interfaces have an appropriate Changeset.\",\n    \"No owned application, domain, test, script or infrastructure workflow retains forbidden mutation or imperative loops. Every necessary host construct has an exact owner/containment/test/removal record; copied reference templates do not provide an escape for executable owned code.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-stable-dependency-qualification.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-version-observations.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-medicare-scope-conflict.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-canonical-skills.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-atom-qualification.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-workflow-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-binding-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-route-policy.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-enforcement-canaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lexical-policy-gaps.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-documentation-tools.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-evaluation-tools.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-artifacts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-credentials.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-workflow-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-receipt-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-file-deadlines.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-retained-deployment-proof.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-inventory-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-typed-lint-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-release-script-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-checking-scripts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-api-app-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-import-checker.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-runtime-tests.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-fixture-deadlines.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-app-hosts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-infrastructure-native-tests.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-web-app-hosts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-hosted-docs-native-proof.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-built-worker-proof.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n  \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-003\",\n    \"CSF-004\",\n    \"CSF-007\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n    \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n    \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n    \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n    \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n    \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n    \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n    \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n    \"bun run api:smoke\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n    \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n    \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n    \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n    \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n    \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n    \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n  \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-001\",\n    \"CSF-004\",\n    \"CSF-005\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Implement every existing catalogue calculator with immutable temporary input/report state, retaining tax rules/results and explicit 2025-26/PAYG limits. Use the Q10-Q12 choices: an explicit Calculate button; edits mark the old answer stale and cancel old work; a main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and sources; a calculator-first homepage with clear developer and agent routes.\",\n    \"Give the SDK an explicit caller-owned lifetime at its plain Promise boundary and an Effect interface; remove the package-global runtime and generic client escapes.\",\n    \"Complete named RPC and public HTTP/OpenAPI operations, bounded body/work/concurrency/rate policy and checked expected failures. Limits and the same safe application owner apply to every transport and caller.\",\n    \"Update package examples, generated snapshots, export/consumer fixtures, supported-scope public copy and Changesets with the new interface.\",\n    \"Tighten retained core/rule/calculator code to the accepted immutable/declarative policy, including one owning Schema and its whole-record checks, fallible constrained constructors, Option for semantic absence with historical codecs preserved, checked configuration, persistent collections, closed named services and flat piping. Do not re-decode checked internal values or use JSON cache keys. Preserve all valid known results; remove only unjustified helper wrappers and keep semantic operation owners.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/web calculator routes/feature containers/leaves and apps/api application operations\",\n    \"packages/calculators/**, packages/core/**, packages/rules/au/*/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/** and packages/sdk/typescript/** owning contracts/exports/tests/examples\",\n    \"Owning package/app READMEs, docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md, frontend.md, effect-services.md and appropriate .changeset/*.md\",\n    \"Local calculator/RPC/HTTP/OpenAPI/SDK consumer and privacy receipts\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/calculators test\",\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n    \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n    \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n    \"bun run api:smoke\",\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run changeset:status\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n    \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n    \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n    \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n    \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6292},"formatted_output":"{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T002\",\n  \"title\": \"Qualify current versions, exports and strict enforcement\",\n  \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n  \"type\": \"foundation\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-001\",\n    \"CSF-002\",\n    \"CSF-010\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T001\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Resolve current official releases, including stable Effect module paths, then qualify one exact Bun/TypeScript/React/Atom/Alchemy/tooling graph in a fresh scratch fixture before integrating it.\",\n    \"Qualify the proposed exact Scheduler peer-metadata correction, or use a newer upstream fix. Preserve valid tax outputs; update package exports/types/imports and versioning consequences deliberately.\",\n    \"Adopt the complete canonical current repository skills (0.6.1 successor of the designed 0.6.0 baseline) and declared TaxKit profiles/receipts, including the required Linear skill folder and Claude link without creating provider projects/issues. Merge all eleven portable strict Effect rules, including no-imperative-collections, and workspace-export direction into the actual lint config across source/tests/tools/config/infrastructure. Reuse baseline mutation/loop/collection checks; add only evidenced gaps and readonly-value checks. Exact Promise-returning/runtime host exceptions do not exempt other constructs.\",\n    \"Extend actual-command positive/negative fixtures under moved paths; assert admitted file counts, exit codes and expected rules. Prove removing/disabling required rules or broadening exact assignment/method exceptions fails the verifier. Refresh Turbo read/input/cache ownership, Knip inventories and CI commands; keep explicit generated/vendor exclusions.\",\n    \"Qualify canonical rejection of let/var, assignments/writes/delete/updates, loops, native array traversal including forEach and mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, switch and manual tag checks. Use existing restrictions and focused corrections for Object/Reflect writes, mutable class/contract values, WeakMap/WeakSet and demonstrated destructured/local aliases. Computed member access is already rejected by no-unchecked-index. Accept persistent collections, pure immutable Effect-managed state and qualified Alchemy Output operations. Preserve/qualify stronger lexical runtime callback/reference checks outside exact hosts. Review helper purpose, Schema ownership and pipe/flat-program call graphs separately; lint alone is not semantic proof.\",\n    \"Cover owned .ts/.tsx/.js/.jsx/.mjs/.cjs files, including retained JavaScript policy tools, in actual lint scope; convert to checked TypeScript where necessary instead of treating the scaffold TypeScript-only override as complete. Executable MDX expressions/imports remain with the existing content-policy owner.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"package.json, bun.lock, turbo.json, tsconfig*, oxlint.config.ts, oxfmt.config.ts, Knip config and .github/workflows/quality.yml\",\n    \"tools/oxlint/** policy/fixtures, tools/effect-language-service/** and tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json\",\n    \"Canonical .agents/skills/** copies with explicit local profiles; AGENTS.md, README.md and affected package READMEs\",\n    \"Qualified version receipt, any exact-version patches/**, applicable .changeset/*.md and owning standards/architecture\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun install --frozen-lockfile\",\n    \"bun run format:check\",\n    \"bun run lint\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run check:effect-language-service\",\n    \"bun run test:skills\",\n    \"bun run check:harness-governance\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Qualify Atom server rendering/hydration, scheduled/cancelled updates, rapid input changes, strict-mode remount and final disposal on the selected React/Scheduler graph.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"The selected graph is actually installed and built; provisional research is not presented as compatibility proof.\",\n    \"Deliberate bad fixtures fail with the expected rule in every owned path group, and documented valid adapters pass.\",\n    \"Retained valid calculations produce unchanged golden results; breaking interfaces have an appropriate Changeset.\",\n    \"No owned application, domain, test, script or infrastructure workflow retains forbidden mutation or imperative loops. Every necessary host construct has an exact owner/containment/test/removal record; copied reference templates do not provide an escape for executable owned code.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-stable-dependency-qualification.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-version-observations.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-medicare-scope-conflict.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-canonical-skills.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-atom-qualification.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-workflow-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-binding-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-route-policy.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-enforcement-canaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lexical-policy-gaps.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-documentation-tools.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-evaluation-tools.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-artifacts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-credentials.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-workflow-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-receipt-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-lint-file-deadlines.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-retained-deployment-proof.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-deployment-inventory-checks.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-typed-lint-policies.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-release-script-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-checking-scripts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-api-app-boundaries.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-import-checker.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-runtime-tests.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-quality-fixture-deadlines.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-docs-app-hosts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-infrastructure-native-tests.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-web-app-hosts.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-hosted-docs-native-proof.json\",\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-built-worker-proof.json\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T003\",\n  \"title\": \"Prove one native API and Website path\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-003\",\n    \"CSF-004\",\n    \"CSF-007\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T002\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Rebuild apps/api as a native Alchemy Worker and apps/web as a standard TanStack Website using one real existing calculator.\",\n    \"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\",\n    \"Qualify checked semantic client errors, malformed-reply handling, safe RPC expected/defect/protocol replies, contract version agreement, credential/redirect/origin policy, one whole-response deadline and earlier caller interruption. Recheck every native fatal/global defect path and unknown-tag/invalid-envelope bypass as well as per-procedure encoding; an outer HTTP reporter, custom procedure defect Schema or codecFor hook alone is insufficient privacy proof. Qualify supported ingress treatment or an exact reviewed native correction where required.\",\n    \"Use native instance/request lifetimes, matching-stage service binding/public address, one Website server runner and a React-owned browser Atom graph; no extra backend runner or Effect Context through TanStack. Bind each host's own origin from native Cloudflare.Worker.URL and cross-host addresses from native resource Outputs, decoded once at application ingress. Missing Outputs fail checked configuration without guessed or concatenated addresses.\",\n    \"Select native Stack.secrets/Doppler at the infrastructure root with explicit stage/precedence; qualify bindings without applying a cloud plan.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/api/src/**, apps/web/src/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/src/** and packages/infrastructure/src/** native composition\",\n    \"alchemy.run.ts and exact stage/secret configuration owners\",\n    \"apps/api/README.md, apps/web/README.md, packages/api/rpc/README.md, packages/api/http/README.md, packages/infrastructure/README.md and affected architecture\",\n    \"Focused client/Worker/lifetime tests and a local two-app receipt\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n    \"bun run api:smoke\",\n    \"bun run check-types\",\n    \"bun run build\",\n    \"bun run test:oxlint\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise initial render and client navigation against the matching local API.\",\n    \"Check actual post-initialisation Worker startup, browser CORS, full response decoding, slow headers/stalled bodies, abort, route change and unmount.\",\n    \"Inspect the production browser bundle for server/Alchemy/provider credentials or live domain implementations.\",\n    \"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\",\n    \"No package/app domain code constructs a runtime or builds a live Layer mid-operation.\",\n    \"The same-stage origin/binding and deadline/cancellation claims have runtime evidence.\",\n    \"Website RPC, HTTP and later MCP reuse one checked application operation. Native RPC wire privacy and failure classification have source/version-matched proof, not assumed defaults or handwritten protocol framing.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"CSF-T004\",\n  \"title\": \"Finish calculator pages and the fresh package interface\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n  \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n  \"requirementIds\": [\n    \"CSF-001\",\n    \"CSF-004\",\n    \"CSF-005\"\n  ],\n  \"dependsOn\": [\n    \"CSF-T003\"\n  ],\n  \"goal\": \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n  \"scope\": [\n    \"Implement every existing catalogue calculator with immutable temporary input/report state, retaining tax rules/results and explicit 2025-26/PAYG limits. Use the Q10-Q12 choices: an explicit Calculate button; edits mark the old answer stale and cancel old work; a main answer with expandable existing breakdown, assumptions, supported year and sources; a calculator-first homepage with clear developer and agent routes.\",\n    \"Give the SDK an explicit caller-owned lifetime at its plain Promise boundary and an Effect interface; remove the package-global runtime and generic client escapes.\",\n    \"Complete named RPC and public HTTP/OpenAPI operations, bounded body/work/concurrency/rate policy and checked expected failures. Limits and the same safe application owner apply to every transport and caller.\",\n    \"Update package examples, generated snapshots, export/consumer fixtures, supported-scope public copy and Changesets with the new interface.\",\n    \"Tighten retained core/rule/calculator code to the accepted immutable/declarative policy, including one owning Schema and its whole-record checks, fallible constrained constructors, Option for semantic absence with historical codecs preserved, checked configuration, persistent collections, closed named services and flat piping. Do not re-decode checked internal values or use JSON cache keys. Preserve all valid known results; remove only unjustified helper wrappers and keep semantic operation owners.\"\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    \"apps/web calculator routes/feature containers/leaves and apps/api application operations\",\n    \"packages/calculators/**, packages/core/**, packages/rules/au/*/**, packages/api/rpc/**, packages/api/http/** and packages/sdk/typescript/** owning contracts/exports/tests/examples\",\n    \"Owning package/app READMEs, docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md, frontend.md, effect-services.md and appropriate .changeset/*.md\",\n    \"Local calculator/RPC/HTTP/OpenAPI/SDK consumer and privacy receipts\"\n  ],\n  \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n  \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/calculators test\",\n    \"bun run --filter=@taxkit/api-http test\",\n    \"bun run sdk:check-packed-artifact\",\n    \"bun run sdk:validate-downstream\",\n    \"bun run api:smoke\",\n    \"bun run test\",\n    \"bun run changeset:status\",\n    \"bun run verification\",\n    \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n  ],\n  \"browserVerification\": [\n    \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n    \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n    \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n  ],\n  \"qualityAudits\": [\n    \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n    \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n    \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n    \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n  ],\n  \"parentAudit\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n    \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n  },\n  \"completionCriteria\": [\n    \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n    \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n    \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n  ],\n  \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\"\n  ]\n}\n"},"started_at_ms":1791126415265,"completed_at_ms":1791126415265}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-04T15:06:55.385Z","ordinal":13091,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a1055e-488d-75e2-ab79-097882eda37b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f32b97e5-93d9-407a-bd4f-b51e1888aa50","process_id":"51972","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,170p' /Users/cooper/.codex/attachments/f82088a9-b579-462a-9bee-4d3685805660/Pasted\\ text.txt"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,170p' /Users/cooper/.codex/attachments/f82088a9-b579-462a-9bee-4d3685805660/Pasted\\ text.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"---\ndocument_type: execution-plan\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: supporting\nowner: taxkit-implementation-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: local continuation, PR reconciliation, approval or dependency revision changes\n---\n\n# TaxKit local continuation prompt\n\nPaste the following into the local thread with this repository selected.\n\n## Task and authority\n\nContinue the approved TaxKit clean-slate improvements tracked in Linear DEV-72\nthrough DEV-81. Work only in `crcorbett/taxkit`. Cooper authorised implementation,\nreviewable commits, pushes, draft PRs and routine Linear tracking. The cloud task\nstopped at Cooper's explicit request to hand off locally; it did not complete the\nwhole rebuild. Do not treat this pause as cancellation or acceptance.\n\nRead `AGENTS.md`, `docs/README.md`, the current Commonplace Linear skill at\n`.agents/skills/linear/SKILL.md` and its applicable references, the strict Effect\nskill, and the relevant package/architecture instructions before editing. Use\n`docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md`, its sibling `.tasks.json`, and\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` as the current scope, dependency,\nacceptance and execution owners. Read live Linear issues, linked design and\ncomments, PR state and hosted checks before resuming. Retain native dependency\nrelations and distinguish implemented, tested, reviewed, merged and deployed.\n\nQ1–Q13 are settled. Cooper's current implementation request supersedes the old\nwhole-design Q14 hold. Do not ask for whole-design permission again. Verify\ntruly unresolved material choices. No merge, deployment, publication or provider\napply is authorised. Final provider-plan approval is a separate boundary.\n\n## Checkout and review stack\n\nFetch remote branches and inspect local changes before switching. The latest\nhandoff branch is `codex/dev-73-skill-test-boundaries`; use its remote HEAD,\nincluding this committed prompt. Review the stack instead of starting again\nfrom main or cherry-picking only its final commit. All listed PRs were drafts,\nunmerged and undeployed at handoff; refresh their live state.\n\n| PR | Branch | Implementation revision |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [88](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/88) | `codex/dev-72-clean-slate-foundation` | `771a506a071277f1f975672c4edaa9e32bf629b0` |\n| [89](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/89) | `codex/dev-73-stable-effect-qualification` | `59b0a36ff1bc6f95501734ee65d789a4f5a37fcc` |\n| [90](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/90) | `codex/dev-73-canonical-skills` | `b726afb556fcafdb929b41417a8b0cf4a4aec92c` |\n| [91](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/91) | `codex/dev-73-atom-and-enforcement` | `8549b92` |\n| [92](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/92) | `codex/dev-73-strict-domain` | `e7b9f0a5a1da09fbc22825ce5916f0ba1d2aac7a` |\n| [93](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/93) | `codex/dev-73-domain-boundaries` | `0b58ab548f1b76d46baf0e65fa5eaacc97f7cb69` |\n| [94](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/94) | `codex/dev-73-owned-collections` | `c8affdc99f5eb155cec1af7793ef8cb8f2feb4cc` |\n| [95](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/95) | `codex/dev-73-effect-tooling-tests` | `8a809208eb87d60575282290dfdd59a681fae676` |\n| [96](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/96) | `codex/dev-73-api-test-boundaries` | `b854aad61e9e8cd07c061584cd2ccbae5e85fc8b` |\n| [97](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/97) | `codex/dev-73-tool-runtime-boundaries` | `3217c6c856da1c599a013d4e3de12722d710000c` |\n| [98](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/98) | `codex/dev-73-docs-adapter-boundaries` | `eb13b36c274b4da017acb170f4505a19caf9a156` |\n\nThe skill-policy migration follows #98 on the handoff branch. Its final PR and\nrevision are recorded in DEV-73 and Git history. PRs #88–98 had passed hosted\nQuality at the cloud readback; #98 run was 37178311127. Recheck the latest branch\nrather than attributing an earlier pass to a later commit.\n\n## Completed scope and remaining goal\n\nDEV-72 retained-work admission is In Review, with Cooper review outstanding.\nDEV-73 remains In Progress. Stable dependency qualification, complete canonical\nskill adoption, real Chromium Atom/Scheduler qualification, immutable core/rule\ncollections, domain/API serialization, shared testing, lint resource ownership,\nrepository-path/governance tooling, docs adapters and skill-policy test migration\nare implemented in the stack. Current receipts under\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/` state each slice's evidence\nand non-claims. Do not mark all of DEV-73 complete based on these slices.\n\nFinish DEV-73's full strict enforcement and host qualification, then implement\nDEV-74–81 in the accepted dependency order through tested reviewable drafts.\nThey have not yet been implemented. Native relations at the previous readback:\n72 → 73 → 74; 75 and 76 depend on 74; 77 depends on 75/76; 78 on 74/76;\n79 on 75/76/77; 80 on 74/75/77; 81 on 78/79/80. Consult the actual task ledger\nfor the full acceptance criteria and reconcile overlap before moving a task.\nDraft PRs are progress checkpoints, not completion of the overall goal.\n\nRemaining T002 work includes SDK and release scripts, documentation/deployment/\nquality/evaluation tooling, executable JavaScript lint policy, app/config and\ninfrastructure paths; exact host exceptions; disabled-rule/exception-broadening\nnegative tests; weak collections, Object/Reflect writes, runtime aliases and\nreadonly contract gaps; and semantic Schema/helper/state/lifetime review.\nThe old provisional inventory was 1,550 strict diagnostics before the docs and\nskill-test slices. It included unqualified host/fixture cases, is not a confirmed\ndefect count, and must be regenerated through the actual installed CLI.\n\nThe SDK still has a package-global ManagedRuntime. T004 explicitly requires\ncaller-owned plain-client lifetime and disposal plus the Effect interface.\nReconcile that accepted design with T002 host enforcement; do not add broad\nruntime exceptions or hide arbitrary execution behind generic callbacks.\n\n## Tax correctness decision and companion repository\n\nProtect retained rules, source artifacts, golden results and all three 2025–26\ncalculators. No Medicare correction was made. Cooper must resolve the bounded\nscope decision recorded in\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-medicare-scope-conflict.json`\nand DEV-73 comment `db7b8f4f-c061-4e79-b12a-4cecd54be0e1`.\n\nAuthoritative enacted source:\nhttps://www.legislation.gov.au/C2026A00058/asmade/2026-06-30/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_1/document_1.html\nAct 58 of 2026 received assent 30 June 2026; Schedule 5 starts 1 July 2026 and\nitem 14 applies to 2025–26 and later assessments. For single non-SAPTO Medicare,\nthe nil threshold changed from $27,222 to $28,011 and the phase-in ceiling from\n$34,027 to $35,013. The 10% phase-in and 2% full rate are unchanged.\nA test-only parameter swap at $30,000 annual taxable income changed the levy\nfrom $277.80 to $198.90 and total tax from $1,465.80 to $1,386.90. At $28,011 the\nlevy changed $78.90 to $0; at $35,013, $700.26 to $700.20 under retained cent\nrounding. $20k/$50k/$80k samples were unchanged. Only the annual income-tax\ncalculator and its downstream representations are affected; PAYG withholding\nand take-home pay use independent Schedule 1 rules. Do not widen to families,\nSAPTO, surcharge or future-year support. Verify any newer decision in Linear\nbefore acting. This decision blocks its correction only, not independent work.\n\nThe exact stable-v4, retained-output revision for companion adad qualification\nis `59b0a36ff1bc6f95501734ee65d789a4f5a37fcc` (#89). It is not a claim of\ncurrent-law Medicare correctness or qualification of later SDK interface changes.\nThe coordinating parent can relay exact companion dependency revisions; adad is\nnot this task's write scope. The old local offline frozen-install failure is\ndistinct from already completed hosted recovery (#86/#87).\n\n## Verification and environment\n\nUse the repository-pinned toolchain and lockfile. The cloud used Bun 1.4.2,\nNode 24.16.0, stable Effect 4.0.0, TypeScript 7.0.2 and @effect/tsgo 0.48.0.\nConsult actual manifests/lockfile for the full graph. Cloud-only activation\n`/workspace/.taxkit-cloud/activate.sh` and `/tmp/taxkit-csf-toolchain` are not\nportable prerequisites; provision the equivalent pinned tools locally.\nCanonical skill trees are pinned to Commonplace development-workflows 0.6.1,\ncommit `91a47d9fdde8aad214a0ab12742517cce344b709`. Do not modify the canonical\nstrict-policy asset to evade enforcement or silently refresh governance hashes.\n\nRun each task's prescribed checks, including frozen install, format, lint,\nactual CLI negative/positive fixtures, types, tests, build, full verification,\nand relevant browser/packed/downstream checks. `bun run test` and\n`bun run verification` cover different gates. Do not run lint/format/type scans\nconcurrently with tests that create temporary rejected source files. Do not edit\ntracked files during release-boundary clone checks. Those tests can be silent\nfor about 90 seconds; full verification typically takes a few minutes. Build\nsequentially before built-app browser tests to avoid output races.\n\nThe latest docs slice passed 75 lint cases and 13 docs-content tests, all tests,\nfull verification, build and local workerd/Chromium proof. The workerd receipt\nharness was corrected to read installed manifests: @cloudflare/vite-plugin\n1.62.5, workerd 1.20261001.1 and Wrangler 4.147.0. Older receipts hard-coded old\nversions and do not establish the current dependency graph; retain them as\nhistory. The processed-text SDK has no abort signal, so interrupting its awaiting\nEffect does not prove provider cancellation. Local workerd is not hosted proof.\n\nReview generated files through their actual owner rather than hand-editing them.\nFumadocs MDX 15.4.6 returns synchronous Vite plugins; Shiki 4.5 consumes the node\nreturned by its pre transformer. Keep provider methods attached to their\nreceiver. Oxlint has no stdin support; use scoped exact-path CLI fixtures.\n`@effect/vitest` exposes `it.effect` (not `test.effect` on its test export).\n\n## Handoff execution\n\nStart by confirming the pushed branch, draft PR, recent CI and clean worktree;\nthen reconcile current Linear. Keep a concrete end-to-end plan through DEV-81,\npost useful milestone/blocker/evidence comments and native project updates,\nand continue safe independent work. Read back writes. Distinguish review,\nimplementation, merge and availability. Keep material unresolved decisions\nvisible without re-requesting already granted implementation authority.\n\nNo native goal-management tool or outbound cloud-thread messaging tool was\navailable in the cloud tool inventory. The goal is recorded in the active plan\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"---\ndocument_type: execution-plan\nlifecycle: current\nauthority: supporting\nowner: taxkit-implementation-owner\nlast_reviewed: 2026-10-04\nreview_trigger: local continuation, PR reconciliation, approval or dependency revision changes\n---\n\n# TaxKit local continuation prompt\n\nPaste the following into the local thread with this repository selected.\n\n## Task and authority\n\nContinue the approved TaxKit clean-slate improvements tracked in Linear DEV-72\nthrough DEV-81. Work only in `crcorbett/taxkit`. Cooper authorised implementation,\nreviewable commits, pushes, draft PRs and routine Linear tracking. The cloud task\nstopped at Cooper's explicit request to hand off locally; it did not complete the\nwhole rebuild. Do not treat this pause as cancellation or acceptance.\n\nRead `AGENTS.md`, `docs/README.md`, the current Commonplace Linear skill at\n`.agents/skills/linear/SKILL.md` and its applicable references, the strict Effect\nskill, and the relevant package/architecture instructions before editing. Use\n`docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md`, its sibling `.tasks.json`, and\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` as the current scope, dependency,\nacceptance and execution owners. Read live Linear issues, linked design and\ncomments, PR state and hosted checks before resuming. Retain native dependency\nrelations and distinguish implemented, tested, reviewed, merged and deployed.\n\nQ1–Q13 are settled. Cooper's current implementation request supersedes the old\nwhole-design Q14 hold. Do not ask for whole-design permission again. Verify\ntruly unresolved material choices. No merge, deployment, publication or provider\napply is authorised. Final provider-plan approval is a separate boundary.\n\n## Checkout and review stack\n\nFetch remote branches and inspect local changes before switching. The latest\nhandoff branch is `codex/dev-73-skill-test-boundaries`; use its remote HEAD,\nincluding this committed prompt. Review the stack instead of starting again\nfrom main or cherry-picking only its final commit. All listed PRs were drafts,\nunmerged and undeployed at handoff; refresh their live state.\n\n| PR | Branch | Implementation revision |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [88](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/88) | `codex/dev-72-clean-slate-foundation` | `771a506a071277f1f975672c4edaa9e32bf629b0` |\n| [89](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/89) | `codex/dev-73-stable-effect-qualification` | `59b0a36ff1bc6f95501734ee65d789a4f5a37fcc` |\n| [90](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/90) | `codex/dev-73-canonical-skills` | `b726afb556fcafdb929b41417a8b0cf4a4aec92c` |\n| [91](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/91) | `codex/dev-73-atom-and-enforcement` | `8549b92` |\n| [92](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/92) | `codex/dev-73-strict-domain` | `e7b9f0a5a1da09fbc22825ce5916f0ba1d2aac7a` |\n| [93](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/93) | `codex/dev-73-domain-boundaries` | `0b58ab548f1b76d46baf0e65fa5eaacc97f7cb69` |\n| [94](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/94) | `codex/dev-73-owned-collections` | `c8affdc99f5eb155cec1af7793ef8cb8f2feb4cc` |\n| [95](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/95) | `codex/dev-73-effect-tooling-tests` | `8a809208eb87d60575282290dfdd59a681fae676` |\n| [96](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/96) | `codex/dev-73-api-test-boundaries` | `b854aad61e9e8cd07c061584cd2ccbae5e85fc8b` |\n| [97](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/97) | `codex/dev-73-tool-runtime-boundaries` | `3217c6c856da1c599a013d4e3de12722d710000c` |\n| [98](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/pull/98) | `codex/dev-73-docs-adapter-boundaries` | `eb13b36c274b4da017acb170f4505a19caf9a156` |\n\nThe skill-policy migration follows #98 on the handoff branch. Its final PR and\nrevision are recorded in DEV-73 and Git history. PRs #88–98 had passed hosted\nQuality at the cloud readback; #98 run was 37178311127. Recheck the latest branch\nrather than attributing an earlier pass to a later commit.\n\n## Completed scope and remaining goal\n\nDEV-72 retained-work admission is In Review, with Cooper review outstanding.\nDEV-73 remains In Progress. Stable dependency qualification, complete canonical\nskill adoption, real Chromium Atom/Scheduler qualification, immutable core/rule\ncollections, domain/API serialization, shared testing, lint resource ownership,\nrepository-path/governance tooling, docs adapters and skill-policy test migration\nare implemented in the stack. Current receipts under\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/` state each slice's evidence\nand non-claims. Do not mark all of DEV-73 complete based on these slices.\n\nFinish DEV-73's full strict enforcement and host qualification, then implement\nDEV-74–81 in the accepted dependency order through tested reviewable drafts.\nThey have not yet been implemented. Native relations at the previous readback:\n72 → 73 → 74; 75 and 76 depend on 74; 77 depends on 75/76; 78 on 74/76;\n79 on 75/76/77; 80 on 74/75/77; 81 on 78/79/80. Consult the actual task ledger\nfor the full acceptance criteria and reconcile overlap before moving a task.\nDraft PRs are progress checkpoints, not completion of the overall goal.\n\nRemaining T002 work includes SDK and release scripts, documentation/deployment/\nquality/evaluation tooling, executable JavaScript lint policy, app/config and\ninfrastructure paths; exact host exceptions; disabled-rule/exception-broadening\nnegative tests; weak collections, Object/Reflect writes, runtime aliases and\nreadonly contract gaps; and semantic Schema/helper/state/lifetime review.\nThe old provisional inventory was 1,550 strict diagnostics before the docs and\nskill-test slices. It included unqualified host/fixture cases, is not a confirmed\ndefect count, and must be regenerated through the actual installed CLI.\n\nThe SDK still has a package-global ManagedRuntime. T004 explicitly requires\ncaller-owned plain-client lifetime and disposal plus the Effect interface.\nReconcile that accepted design with T002 host enforcement; do not add broad\nruntime exceptions or hide arbitrary execution behind generic callbacks.\n\n## Tax correctness decision and companion repository\n\nProtect retained rules, source artifacts, golden results and all three 2025–26\ncalculators. No Medicare correction was made. Cooper must resolve the bounded\nscope decision recorded in\n`docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-medicare-scope-conflict.json`\nand DEV-73 comment `db7b8f4f-c061-4e79-b12a-4cecd54be0e1`.\n\nAuthoritative enacted source:\nhttps://www.legislation.gov.au/C2026A00058/asmade/2026-06-30/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_1/document_1.html\nAct 58 of 2026 received assent 30 June 2026; Schedule 5 starts 1 July 2026 and\nitem 14 applies to 2025–26 and later assessments. For single non-SAPTO Medicare,\nthe nil threshold changed from $27,222 to $28,011 and the phase-in ceiling from\n$34,027 to $35,013. The 10% phase-in and 2% full rate are unchanged.\nA test-only parameter swap at $30,000 annual taxable income changed the levy\nfrom $277.80 to $198.90 and total tax from $1,465.80 to $1,386.90. At $28,011 the\nlevy changed $78.90 to $0; at $35,013, $700.26 to $700.20 under retained cent\nrounding. $20k/$50k/$80k samples were unchanged. Only the annual income-tax\ncalculator and its downstream representations are affected; PAYG withholding\nand take-home pay use independent Schedule 1 rules. Do not widen to families,\nSAPTO, surcharge or future-year support. Verify any newer decision in Linear\nbefore acting. This decision blocks its correction only, not independent work.\n\nThe exact stable-v4, retained-output revision for companion adad qualification\nis `59b0a36ff1bc6f95501734ee65d789a4f5a37fcc` (#89). It is not a claim of\ncurrent-law Medicare correctness or qualification of later SDK interface changes.\nThe coordinating parent can relay exact companion dependency revisions; adad is\nnot this task's write scope. The old local offline frozen-install failure is\ndistinct from already completed hosted recovery (#86/#87).\n\n## Verification and environment\n\nUse the repository-pinned toolchain and lockfile. The cloud used Bun 1.4.2,\nNode 24.16.0, stable Effect 4.0.0, TypeScript 7.0.2 and @effect/tsgo 0.48.0.\n