uted lint-only inputs preserve isolated host/binding-rule contexts; neighbouring files remain strict','Actual six-extension and five-neighbour admission/rejection controls with exact file count and expected rules','Valid CommonJS positive/negative fixtures, separately from ESM syntax','Two new isolated real-verifier mutations reject removed whole-source coverage and broadened fixture exclusions; existing controls/deadlines preserved'],'checks':[],'documentation_impact':{'Change required':['oxlint.config.ts','tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts','tools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts','tools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts','tools/quality-workflow/fixtures/strict-enforcement-defects.json','docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md','docs/standards/controls.md','docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md','docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json'],'Preserve':['All canonical rule severities and narrow runtime/codec/assignment/method admissions','Explicit generated/vendor exclusions and MDX expression owner','Canonical skills/digests, installed dependencies, public content, historical evidence, provider state and retained tax results'],'N/A':{'Changeset':'repository tooling only; no package contract change','runbook/provider operation':'same local verification commands; no consequential operation','new public/generated output':'unchanged'}},'fixture_containment':{'paths':['tools/oxlint/fixtures/bun-accepted.ts','tools/oxlint/fixtures/bun-global-non-host-accepted.ts','tools/oxlint/fixtures/bun-unrelated-accepted.ts','tools/oxlint/fixtures/effect-accepted.ts','tools/oxlint/fixtures/effect-unrelated-accepted.ts'],'purpose':'unexecuted source inputs read by the actual lint corpus to isolate separate binding/host rules','owner':'tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts','compiler_boundary':'tools/oxlint/tsconfig.json includes only ./*.ts, outside fixtures directory','removal':'retire exact exclusions when their isolated rule fixtures are retired; no workflow host admission'},'recovery':{'failed_observations':['Initial new test object was unsorted, corrected','Initial CommonJS corpus used ESM imports and failed the strict diagnostic Schema before rule assertions; replaced with valid CommonJS fixtures','Initial corpus extension edit duplicated two expected IDs; corrected before isolated verification'],'rollback':'revert this complete slice to parent revision','resume_trigger':'finish local qualification and parent semantic review before accepting T002; then DEV-74–81','next_owner':'TaxKit implementation owner'},'limitations':['Whole-repository qualification and new isolated controls pending','No merge/deployment/publication/provider apply/version application','DEV-73 remains in progress; Medicare separate'],'postconditions':[],'logs_location':'Task-local pinned-toolchain directory, portable basenames only'},indent=2)+'\\n')\np=Path('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text());next(t for t in d['tasks'] if t['id']=='CSF-T002')['evidence'].append(receipt);p.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\n')\np=Path('docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md');s=p.read_text();s+='''\n\n### Whole-source strict coverage — implementation in progress, 2026-10-05\n\nThis slice follows draft #125 revision\n`cd5b2a8dec1fdd53375486852485a898215d9ede`. Its hosted Quality run\n`37212184618` remains in progress at the last readback; local qualification is\nrecorded separately. The canonical override covers all six owned source\nextensions, including future root/app/config/tool files. Exactly five named,\nunexecuted lint inputs retain their isolated rule contexts; directories and\nneighbours remain strict, and other rules still inspect those inputs. Existing\nruntime/codec/assignment/method admissions and generated/vendor exclusions are\nunchanged. These inputs sit outside the policy compiler's ./*.ts ownership and\nare read as source bytes, never executed as app/tool workflows.\n\nActual CLI checks cover all six extensions and five fixture neighbours, with\none-file admission, nonzero exit and named rules. The first CommonJS input used\nES-module syntax and failed before the intended rules; valid CommonJS positive/\nnegative inputs correct that oracle. All 401 lint cases pass after correction.\nTwo new independent repository-copy checks remove whole-source coverage or\nbroaden fixture exclusions and must fail the complete real verifier. The six\nstrict and six retained release-boundary mutations keep their five-minute\nlimits. Full qualification and the final T002 semantic review remain pending.\n\nDocumentation impact: **Change required** for lint/test/Quality owners, testing\narchitecture, controls standard, this plan/T002 and the\n[receipt](../../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-owned-source-coverage.json).\n**Preserve** canonical rules/skills/digests, exact host admissions, dependencies,\npublic/generated content, prior evidence, provider state and tax results.\n**N/A** Changeset (repository tooling only), new runbook/provider operation and\npublic contract. No merge/deployment/publication/provider apply/version\napplication. DEV-73 remains in progress; Medicare separate.\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\nPATH=/private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/bun-darwin-aarch64:$PATH node_modules/.bin/oxfmt -c oxfmt.config.ts --write oxlint.config.ts tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts tools/oxlint/fixtures/strict-commonjs-accepted.cjs tools/quality-workflow/release-boundary.test.ts tools/quality-workflow/schemas.ts > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/owned-source-pre-qualification-format.log 2>&1\nPATH=/private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/bun-darwin-aarch64:$PATH bun run lint > /private/tmp/taxkit-local-toolchain/owned-source-root-lint.log 2>&1"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":3,"nanos":914314417},"formatted_output":""},"started_at_ms":1791127210094,"c